  "_metadata": {
    "title": "Dan - Solo Estate Lawyer Plan",
    "narrative": "This is a story about Dan, a divorced 54-year-old estate lawyer with no friends and no dependents. Born on September 12, 1971, Dan currently makes $190,000 per year and has accumulated a solid nest egg: $1.2M in RRSPs, $100K in TFSAs, $250K in a Non-Registered account, and $50K in a High Interest Savings Account (HISA). Dan plans to retire on his 60th birthday (September 12, 2031). He aims for a quiet retirement with flat spending of $60,000 per year (inflation-adjusted) until he dies at age 82. Since he has no dependents, his goal is simply to ensure his own security without worrying about leaving an estate. He will save $20,000/year in RRSPs and $7,000/year in TFSAs until retirement, and then stop all contributions. We assume a flat 8.0% nominal return on investments and a 2.0% return on his HISA. He will take his maximum CPP and full OAS benefits at age 65."
